<title>USA: USDA offers GSM-103 credits to Peru for livestock.</title>
<headline>USDA offers GSM-103 credits to Peru for livestock.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-11-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. Agriculture Department said Friday it offered $5 million in intermediate-term GSM-103 export credit guarantees for the sale of breeder livestock to Peru.</p>
<p>The credit guarantees would be available first-come, first-served for selling breeding cattle, swine, sheep, goats, horses and donkeys. Semen and embryos are eligible too.</p>
<p>Under the offer, coverage of up to 98 percent of the principal involved in a sale was available for three to five years.</p>
